AWSTemplateFormatVersion: "2010-09-09"

Description: >-
  Cost controls for the shared instructor-account Bedrock API key. Deploys into
  the configured instructor account in us-east-1.

  Three controls, in order of how fast they act. A CloudWatch circuit breaker
  deactivates the shared credential within about 90 seconds of a runaway. Bedrock
  model invocation logging records what was sent, so a postmortem can name the
  notebook cell that ran away. An AWS Budget mails the instructor when the
  account's Bedrock spend crosses a threshold, hours later.

  Deploy with uv run bedrock-key/admin.py deploy, which reads every parameter
  value from bedrock-key/arns.env. Do not deploy this file by hand, because the
  parameter defaults below are deliberately absent for values that must match
  the live credential.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why the breaker measures dollars rather than calls
#
# The burn is denominated in tokens, not in requests. One InvokeModel call can
# carry two hundred tokens or two hundred thousand, so an alarm on Invocations
# has no fixed relationship to money and would need a threshold that is wrong
# by three orders of magnitude in one direction or the other.
#
# A raw token count is closer but still wrong, because the three workshop models
# are not priced alike. Claude Sonnet 4.6 output costs $15 per million tokens.
# Titan Text Embeddings V2 input costs $0.02 per million. A token-count alarm
# sized for chat would never see an embedding runaway, and a token-count alarm
# sized for embeddings would trip on the Module 1 ingest burst, which is
# legitimate work that costs under a cent per minute.
#
# So the breaker alarms on a CloudWatch metric math expression that weights each
# model's token counts by that model's published price and yields estimated US
# dollars per minute. That is the unit the threshold is reasoned about in, the
# unit the operator sees on the dashboard, and the unit the budget is written in.
#
# Measured 2026-08-26 with cloudwatch:ListMetrics against account ${BEDROCK_KEY_ACCOUNT_ID}:
# the cross-region profile publishes under ModelId "us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6"
# in us-east-1 only, not under the underlying foundation-model id and not in the
# us-east-2 or us-west-2 fan-out regions. One alarm in us-east-1 therefore sees
# the whole chat spend. The same call found unrelated Sonnet 5 and global-profile
# traffic in this account, which is why every metric below is pinned to a
# ModelId dimension instead of using the account-wide rollup.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Parameters:

  KeyUserName:
    Type: String
    Description: IAM user that owns the shared Bedrock key. From BEDROCK_KEY_USER_NAME.

  KeyCredentialId:
    Type: String
    AllowedPattern: "^ACCA[A-Z0-9]+$"
    Description: >-
      Service-specific credential id the breaker deactivates. From
      BEDROCK_KEY_CREDENTIAL_ID. This is an identifier, not a secret.

  ChatModelId:
    Type: String
    Description: Cross-region chat profile id. From WORKSHOP_CHAT_MODEL_ID.

  EmbedModelId:
    Type: String
    Description: Retrieval embedding model id. From WORKSHOP_EMBED_MODEL_ID.

  MemoryEmbedModelId:
    Type: String
    Description: Agent-memory embedding model id. From WORKSHOP_MEMORY_EMBED_MODEL_ID.

  AlertEmail:
    Type: String
    Description: >-
      Address that receives the breaker notice and every budget alert. From
      BEDROCK_KEY_ALERT_EMAIL. admin.py manages the SNS email subscription and
      confirms it with authenticated unsubscribe protection. The budget also
      sends directly to this address.

  InvocationLogGroupName:
    Type: String
    Default: /aws/bedrock/graphrag-workshop-invocations
    Description: From BEDROCK_KEY_INVOCATION_LOG_GROUP.

  InvocationLogRetentionDays:
    Type: Number
    Default: 14
    AllowedValues: [1, 3, 5, 7, 14, 30, 60, 90]
    Description: >-
      Invocation logging records prompts and completions verbatim, so this group
      holds student-authored text. Fourteen days is the shortest retention that
      still covers a postmortem in the week after a Thursday class. Anything
      longer keeps student text with no operational use for it.

  # The four tuning knobs. admin.py deploy sets all four from arns.env, so
  # a threshold change is an edit to arns.env and a redeploy, never an edit to
  # this file. The bounds below exist so a typo cannot deploy a nonsense
  # breaker. CONTROLS.md carries the arithmetic behind the defaults.
  BurstThresholdUsdPerMinute:
    Type: Number
    Default: 30
    MinValue: 1
    MaxValue: 500
    Description: >-
      One minute above this estimated spend rate deactivates the key. Set from
      BEDROCK_KEY_BURST_USD_PER_MINUTE. The floor is 1 rather than 0 because a
      threshold of 0 deactivates the key on the first token anyone sends.

  SustainedThresholdUsdPerMinute:
    Type: Number
    Default: 25
    MinValue: 1
    MaxValue: 500
    Description: >-
      A run of consecutive five-minute periods each averaging above this rate
      deactivates the key. Set from BEDROCK_KEY_SUSTAINED_USD_PER_MINUTE. The
      run length is SustainedEvaluationPeriods. This catches a slow burn that
      never touches the burst threshold. Keep it below the burst threshold.
      admin.py refuses to deploy if it is not.

  SustainedEvaluationPeriods:
    Type: Number
    Default: 3
    MinValue: 2
    MaxValue: 24
    Description: >-
      How many consecutive five-minute periods the sustained alarm needs before
      it trips. Set from BEDROCK_KEY_SUSTAINED_PERIODS. Three periods is fifteen
      minutes. The floor is 2 because a one-period sustained alarm is only a
      slower burst alarm.

  WorkshopTotalUsd:
    Type: Number
    Default: 850
    MinValue: 0.000001
    MaxValue: 100000
    Description: >-
      Estimated spend across the workshop models in the trailing four hours
      that deactivates the key. Set from BEDROCK_KEY_TOTAL_USD. This is a trip
      threshold rather than a guaranteed billing ceiling, so leave room for
      metric publication, alarm delivery, and calls already in flight.

  MonthlyBudgetUsd:
    Type: Number
    Default: 800
    Description: Account-wide Bedrock cost budget for the month of the class.

  BudgetServiceFilters:
    Type: CommaDelimitedList
    Default: "Amazon Bedrock,Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Amazon Bedrock Edition)"
    Description: >-
      Cost Explorer SERVICE dimension values the budget counts. Third-party
      models on Bedrock bill under their own service value, not under "Amazon
      Bedrock", so a budget naming only "Amazon Bedrock" would miss every dollar
      of chat spend and count only the embeddings. Measured with
      ce:GetDimensionValues against account ${BEDROCK_KEY_ACCOUNT_ID} on 2026-08-26, which
      returned four values: "Amazon Bedrock", "Amazon Bedrock AgentCore",
      "Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Amazon Bedrock Edition)", and "Claude Sonnet 5
      (Amazon Bedrock Edition)". The two omitted values are unrelated account
      work. Re-read the list if the workshop's model set changes.

  ChatInputUsdPerMillion:
    Type: Number
    Default: 3
    Description: >-
      Assumed Claude Sonnet 4.6 input rate. The AWS Price List API returns no
      us-east-1 row for a us. cross-region profile, so this is the first-party
      published rate rather than a measured one.

  ChatOutputUsdPerMillion:
    Type: Number
    Default: 15
    Description: Assumed Claude Sonnet 4.6 output rate. Same caveat as the input rate.

  EmbedUsdPerMillion:
    Type: Number
    Default: 0.135
    Description: >-
      Nova 2 Multimodal Embeddings text input. Measured from the AWS Price List
      API on 2026-08-26 as $0.000135 per 1K tokens.

  MemoryEmbedUsdPerMillion:
    Type: Number
    Default: 0.02
    Description: >-
      Titan Text Embeddings V2 input. Measured from the AWS Price List API on
      2026-08-26 as $0.00002 per 1K tokens.

Resources:

  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Notification path. The alarm cannot call IAM, so it publishes to SNS, SNS
  # invokes the breaker Lambda, and the Lambda calls IAM.
  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------

  BreakerTopic:
    Type: AWS::SNS::Topic
    Properties:
      TopicName: !Sub "${AWS::StackName}-breaker"
      DisplayName: Workshop Bedrock key breaker
      Tags:
        - Key: WorkshopResource
          Value: graphrag-with-neo4j

  BreakerTopicPolicy:
    Type: AWS::SNS::TopicPolicy
    Properties:
      Topics:
        - !Ref BreakerTopic
      PolicyDocument:
        Version: "2012-10-17"
        Statement:
          - Sid: AllowCloudWatchAlarmsToPublish
            Effect: Allow
            Principal:
              Service: cloudwatch.amazonaws.com
            Action: sns:Publish
            Resource: !Ref BreakerTopic
            Condition:
              StringEquals:
                AWS:SourceAccount: !Ref AWS::AccountId

  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # The breaker Lambda.
  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Created explicitly so the execution role's logs grant can name one group
  # rather than every group in the account.
  BreakerFunctionLogGroup:
    Type: AWS::Logs::LogGroup
    DeletionPolicy: Delete
    UpdateReplacePolicy: Delete
    Properties:
      LogGroupName: !Sub "/aws/lambda/${AWS::StackName}-breaker"
      RetentionInDays: 14

  BreakerFunctionRole:
    Type: AWS::IAM::Role
    Properties:
      AssumeRolePolicyDocument:
        Version: "2012-10-17"
        Statement:
          - Effect: Allow
            Principal:
              Service: lambda.amazonaws.com
            Action: sts:AssumeRole
      Policies:
        - PolicyName: deactivate-one-bedrock-key
          PolicyDocument:
            Version: "2012-10-17"
            Statement:
              # iam:UpdateServiceSpecificCredential accepts only the "user"
              # resource type, and its one condition key is
              # iam:ServiceSpecificCredentialServiceName. Verified against the
              # AWS IAM service reference on 2026-08-26. IAM has no condition
              # key for a credential id, so the tightest grant expressible is
              # one action, on one user, for one service name. The credential id
              # itself is pinned in the function's environment and is the only
              # id the code ever passes.
              - Sid: DeactivateTheSharedBedrockKeyOnly
                Effect: Allow
                Action: iam:UpdateServiceSpecificCredential
                Resource: !Sub "arn:${AWS::Partition}:iam::${AWS::AccountId}:user/workshop/${KeyUserName}"
                Condition:
                  StringEquals:
                    iam:ServiceSpecificCredentialServiceName: bedrock.amazonaws.com
              # The Arn attribute of a log group already ends in ":*", which is
              # the every-stream-in-this-group form. Appending a second ":*"
              # produced ":*:*" and matched only by wildcard luck.
              - Sid: WriteOwnLogsOnly
                Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - logs:CreateLogStream
                  - logs:PutLogEvents
                Resource: !GetAtt BreakerFunctionLogGroup.Arn
      Tags:
        - Key: WorkshopResource
          Value: graphrag-with-neo4j

  BreakerFunction:
    Type: AWS::Lambda::Function
    DependsOn: BreakerFunctionLogGroup
    Properties:
      FunctionName: !Sub "${AWS::StackName}-breaker"
      Description: Deactivates the shared workshop Bedrock key when a spend alarm fires.
      Runtime: python3.13
      Handler: index.handler
      Timeout: 30
      MemorySize: 256
      Role: !GetAtt BreakerFunctionRole.Arn
      Environment:
        Variables:
          KEY_USER_NAME: !Ref KeyUserName
          KEY_CREDENTIAL_ID: !Ref KeyCredentialId
      Tags:
        - Key: WorkshopResource
          Value: graphrag-with-neo4j
      Code:
        ZipFile: |
          """Deactivate the shared workshop Bedrock key when a spend alarm fires.

          The alarm cannot call IAM, so it publishes to SNS and SNS invokes this
          function. The one write it performs is scoped by the execution role to
          iam:UpdateServiceSpecificCredential on one user, and the credential id
          comes from the environment rather than from the event, so a malformed
          or spoofed SNS message cannot redirect it at another credential.

          Nothing here catches the IAM error. A failed deactivation must surface
          as a Lambda error so SNS retries it and the failure is visible in the
          function's metrics. Swallowing it would report a stop that never
          happened, which is the one failure mode this control cannot have.
          """

          import json
          import logging
          import os

          import boto3

          LOG = logging.getLogger()
          LOG.setLevel(logging.INFO)

          USER_NAME = os.environ["KEY_USER_NAME"]
          CREDENTIAL_ID = os.environ["KEY_CREDENTIAL_ID"]

          _iam = boto3.client("iam")


          def alarm_name(record: dict) -> str:
              """Return the alarm name carried in one SNS record."""
              try:
                  message = json.loads(record["Sns"]["Message"])
              except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError):
                  return "unparsed-sns-record"
              return message.get("AlarmName", "unnamed-alarm")


          def handler(event: dict, context: object) -> dict:
              """Set the shared Bedrock credential to Inactive."""
              names = [alarm_name(r) for r in event.get("Records", [])]
              LOG.info("tripped by: %s", ", ".join(names) or "no SNS record")
              _iam.update_service_specific_credential(
                  UserName=USER_NAME,
                  ServiceSpecificCredentialId=CREDENTIAL_ID,
                  Status="Inactive",
              )
              LOG.warning(
                  "deactivated credential %s on user %s", CREDENTIAL_ID, USER_NAME
              )
              return {
                  "credentialId": CREDENTIAL_ID,
                  "status": "Inactive",
                  "alarms": names,
              }

  BreakerFunctionInvokePermission:
    Type: AWS::Lambda::Permission
    Properties:
      FunctionName: !GetAtt BreakerFunction.Arn
      Action: lambda:InvokeFunction
      Principal: sns.amazonaws.com
      SourceArn: !Ref BreakerTopic

  # DependsOn the permission, so the topic can never hold a subscription it is
  # not yet allowed to deliver to.
  #
  # The filter policy is what keeps BreakerFailureAlarm off this subscription.
  # Four alarms publish to this topic and only three of them should reach the
  # Lambda. Without the filter, the alarm that reports a broken breaker would
  # invoke the breaker again. The email subscription managed by admin.py carries
  # no filter, so the operator still receives all four.
  #
  # All names come from Ref against the alarm resources, so the filter cannot
  # drift away from the alarms it names. Confirm it end to end with the
  # set-alarm-state rehearsal in CONTROLS.md before class.
  BreakerFunctionSubscription:
    Type: AWS::SNS::Subscription
    DependsOn: BreakerFunctionInvokePermission
    Properties:
      TopicArn: !Ref BreakerTopic
      Protocol: lambda
      Endpoint: !GetAtt BreakerFunction.Arn
      FilterPolicyScope: MessageBody
      FilterPolicy:
        AlarmName:
          - !Ref BurstSpendAlarm
          - !Ref SustainedSpendAlarm
          - !Ref WorkshopTotalSpendAlarm

  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # The three spend alarms evaluate the same price-weighted expression over one
  # minute, fifteen minutes, or a rolling four hours. None has an OKAction.
  # Bringing the key back must be a human decision, because an automatic
  # recovery would restart the same runaway loop the breaker just stopped.
  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------

  BurstSpendAlarm:
    Type: AWS::CloudWatch::Alarm
    Properties:
      AlarmName: !Sub "${AWS::StackName}-burst-spend"
      AlarmDescription: >-
        Estimated Bedrock spend across the three workshop models exceeded the
        burst threshold in a single minute. The breaker Lambda has deactivated
        the shared key. See bedrock-key/README.md.
      ComparisonOperator: GreaterThanThreshold
      Threshold: !Ref BurstThresholdUsdPerMinute
      EvaluationPeriods: 1
      DatapointsToAlarm: 1
      TreatMissingData: notBreaching
      ActionsEnabled: true
      AlarmActions:
        - !Ref BreakerTopic
      Metrics:
        - Id: chat_in
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 60
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: InputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref ChatModelId
        - Id: chat_out
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 60
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: OutputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref ChatModelId
        - Id: embed_in
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 60
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: InputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref EmbedModelId
        - Id: memory_in
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 60
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: InputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref MemoryEmbedModelId
        - Id: usd_per_minute
          ReturnData: true
          Label: Estimated USD per minute, workshop models
          Expression: !Sub >-
            (FILL(chat_in,0)*${ChatInputUsdPerMillion}
            + FILL(chat_out,0)*${ChatOutputUsdPerMillion}
            + FILL(embed_in,0)*${EmbedUsdPerMillion}
            + FILL(memory_in,0)*${MemoryEmbedUsdPerMillion}) / 1000000

  SustainedSpendAlarm:
    Type: AWS::CloudWatch::Alarm
    Properties:
      AlarmName: !Sub "${AWS::StackName}-sustained-spend"
      AlarmDescription: >-
        Estimated Bedrock spend averaged above the sustained threshold for every
        one of SustainedEvaluationPeriods consecutive five-minute periods. The
        breaker Lambda has deactivated the shared key. See
        bedrock-key/README.md.
      ComparisonOperator: GreaterThanThreshold
      Threshold: !Ref SustainedThresholdUsdPerMinute
      EvaluationPeriods: !Ref SustainedEvaluationPeriods
      DatapointsToAlarm: !Ref SustainedEvaluationPeriods
      TreatMissingData: notBreaching
      ActionsEnabled: true
      AlarmActions:
        - !Ref BreakerTopic
      Metrics:
        - Id: chat_in
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 300
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: InputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref ChatModelId
        - Id: chat_out
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 300
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: OutputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref ChatModelId
        - Id: embed_in
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 300
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: InputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref EmbedModelId
        - Id: memory_in
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 300
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: InputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref MemoryEmbedModelId
        # Divided by five so a 300-second window reports the same unit the burst
        # alarm reports. Both thresholds are then read as dollars per minute.
        - Id: usd_per_minute
          ReturnData: true
          Label: Estimated USD per minute, five-minute average
          Expression: !Sub >-
            (FILL(chat_in,0)*${ChatInputUsdPerMillion}
            + FILL(chat_out,0)*${ChatOutputUsdPerMillion}
            + FILL(embed_in,0)*${EmbedUsdPerMillion}
            + FILL(memory_in,0)*${MemoryEmbedUsdPerMillion}) / 5000000

  WorkshopTotalSpendAlarm:
    Type: AWS::CloudWatch::Alarm
    Properties:
      AlarmName: !Sub "${AWS::StackName}-workshop-total-spend"
      AlarmDescription: >-
        Estimated Bedrock spend across the workshop models exceeded the
        configured total in the trailing four hours. The breaker Lambda has
        deactivated the shared key. See bedrock-key/README.md.
      ComparisonOperator: GreaterThanThreshold
      Threshold: !Ref WorkshopTotalUsd
      EvaluationPeriods: 1
      DatapointsToAlarm: 1
      # EvaluationWindow is omitted intentionally. CloudWatch's default is a
      # sliding window; a wall-clock window could reset during the workshop.
      TreatMissingData: notBreaching
      ActionsEnabled: true
      AlarmActions:
        - !Ref BreakerTopic
      Metrics:
        - Id: chat_in
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 14400
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: InputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref ChatModelId
        - Id: chat_out
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 14400
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: OutputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref ChatModelId
        - Id: embed_in
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 14400
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: InputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref EmbedModelId
        - Id: memory_in
          ReturnData: false
          MetricStat:
            Period: 14400
            Stat: Sum
            Metric:
              Namespace: AWS/Bedrock
              MetricName: InputTokenCount
              Dimensions:
                - Name: ModelId
                  Value: !Ref MemoryEmbedModelId
        - Id: rolling_usd
          ReturnData: true
          Label: Estimated USD, trailing four hours
          Expression: !Sub >-
            (FILL(chat_in,0)*${ChatInputUsdPerMillion}
            + FILL(chat_out,0)*${ChatOutputUsdPerMillion}
            + FILL(embed_in,0)*${EmbedUsdPerMillion}
            + FILL(memory_in,0)*${MemoryEmbedUsdPerMillion}) / 1000000

  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Did the breaker actually work?
  #
  # The email subscription and the Lambda subscription are independent. A spend
  # alarm mails the operator whether or not the Lambda's IAM call succeeded, so
  # an operator reading only the email would believe the key is off while it is
  # still live. This alarm closes that gap. Any Lambda error inside one minute
  # produces a second mail, and that second mail means go and read the
  # credential status by hand.
  #
  # It notifies and nothing else. There is no OKAction and no second action. It
  # publishes to BreakerTopic so it reaches the same inbox with no second
  # confirmation workflow to duplicate, and BreakerFunctionSubscription's filter
  # policy names only the three spend alarms, so this alarm's message reaches the
  # email and never the Lambda. A breaker that re-triggered itself on its own
  # failure is the loop that filter exists to prevent.
  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------

  BreakerFailureAlarm:
    Type: AWS::CloudWatch::Alarm
    Properties:
      AlarmName: !Sub "${AWS::StackName}-breaker-failed"
      AlarmDescription: >-
        The breaker Lambda raised an error, so the shared key may still be
        Active after a spend alarm fired. Read the credential status by hand and
        stop it with uv run bedrock-key/admin.py stop if it is still Active.
        See bedrock-key/CONTROLS.md.
      Namespace: AWS/Lambda
      MetricName: Errors
      Dimensions:
        - Name: FunctionName
          Value: !Ref BreakerFunction
      Statistic: Sum
      Period: 60
      ComparisonOperator: GreaterThanThreshold
      Threshold: 0
      EvaluationPeriods: 1
      DatapointsToAlarm: 1
      # A minute with no invocation publishes no datapoint. That is the normal
      # state of this function and must never read as a failure.
      TreatMissingData: notBreaching
      ActionsEnabled: true
      AlarmActions:
        - !Ref BreakerTopic

  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # The class-day view. README.md sends the operator here and nowhere else.
  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------

  SpendDashboard:
    Type: AWS::CloudWatch::Dashboard
    Properties:
      DashboardName: !Sub "${AWS::StackName}"
      DashboardBody: !Sub |
        {
          "widgets": [
            {
              "type": "metric",
              "x": 0, "y": 0, "width": 24, "height": 8,
              "properties": {
                "title": "Estimated Bedrock spend, USD per minute",
                "region": "${AWS::Region}",
                "view": "timeSeries",
                "stacked": false,
                "period": 60,
                "stat": "Sum",
                "yAxis": { "left": { "min": 0, "showUnits": false, "label": "USD/min" } },
                "annotations": {
                  "horizontal": [
                    {
                      "label": "sustained trip, 15 min average",
                      "value": ${SustainedThresholdUsdPerMinute},
                      "color": "#ff7f0e"
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "burst trip, 1 min",
                      "value": ${BurstThresholdUsdPerMinute},
                      "color": "#d62728"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "metrics": [
                  [ { "expression": "(FILL(m1,0)*${ChatInputUsdPerMillion} + FILL(m2,0)*${ChatOutputUsdPerMillion} + FILL(m3,0)*${EmbedUsdPerMillion} + FILL(m4,0)*${MemoryEmbedUsdPerMillion}) / 1000000", "label": "USD per minute", "id": "e1", "region": "${AWS::Region}", "color": "#1f77b4" } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "InputTokenCount", "ModelId", "${ChatModelId}", { "id": "m1", "visible": false } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "OutputTokenCount", "ModelId", "${ChatModelId}", { "id": "m2", "visible": false } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "InputTokenCount", "ModelId", "${EmbedModelId}", { "id": "m3", "visible": false } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "InputTokenCount", "ModelId", "${MemoryEmbedModelId}", { "id": "m4", "visible": false } ]
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "metric",
              "x": 0, "y": 8, "width": 12, "height": 7,
              "properties": {
                "title": "Tokens per minute by model",
                "region": "${AWS::Region}",
                "view": "timeSeries",
                "stacked": false,
                "period": 60,
                "stat": "Sum",
                "yAxis": { "left": { "min": 0, "showUnits": false, "label": "tokens/min" } },
                "metrics": [
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "InputTokenCount", "ModelId", "${ChatModelId}", { "label": "chat input" } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "OutputTokenCount", "ModelId", "${ChatModelId}", { "label": "chat output" } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "InputTokenCount", "ModelId", "${EmbedModelId}", { "label": "retrieval embeddings" } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "InputTokenCount", "ModelId", "${MemoryEmbedModelId}", { "label": "memory embeddings" } ]
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "metric",
              "x": 12, "y": 8, "width": 12, "height": 7,
              "properties": {
                "title": "Calls, throttles, and client errors per minute",
                "region": "${AWS::Region}",
                "view": "timeSeries",
                "stacked": false,
                "period": 60,
                "stat": "Sum",
                "yAxis": { "left": { "min": 0, "showUnits": false, "label": "count/min" } },
                "metrics": [
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "Invocations", "ModelId", "${ChatModelId}", { "label": "chat calls" } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "Invocations", "ModelId", "${EmbedModelId}", { "label": "retrieval embed calls" } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "Invocations", "ModelId", "${MemoryEmbedModelId}", { "label": "memory embed calls" } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "InvocationThrottles", "ModelId", "${ChatModelId}", { "label": "chat throttles", "color": "#ff7f0e" } ],
                  [ "AWS/Bedrock", "InvocationClientErrors", "ModelId", "${ChatModelId}", { "label": "chat client errors", "color": "#d62728" } ]
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }

  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Model invocation logging.
  #
  # Invocation logging records the request and response bodies verbatim, which
  # means this group holds the prompts students typed and the completions the
  # model returned. Treat it as student-authored text. Retention is set from
  # InvocationLogRetentionDays and defaults to 14 days, which covers a postmortem
  # in the week after class and keeps nothing beyond that.
  #
  # Only text delivery is enabled. Embedding delivery would write every embedded
  # chunk from forty students into this group for no diagnostic value, and image
  # and video are modalities this workshop never sends.
  #
  # No largeDataDeliveryS3Config is configured, so a request or response body
  # over 100 KB is not delivered. That is acceptable here, because the purpose is
  # to identify which prompt shape ran away, not to keep a complete archive.
  #
  # This does not give per-student attribution. Every log record's identity.arn
  # is the one shared key user, because every student sends the same bearer
  # token. The prompt text is what tells you which module or which loop ran away.
  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------

  InvocationLogGroup:
    Type: AWS::Logs::LogGroup
    DeletionPolicy: Delete
    UpdateReplacePolicy: Delete
    Properties:
      LogGroupName: !Ref InvocationLogGroupName
      RetentionInDays: !Ref InvocationLogRetentionDays
      Tags:
        - Key: WorkshopResource
          Value: graphrag-with-neo4j
        - Key: Contains
          Value: student-authored-text

  InvocationLogRole:
    Type: AWS::IAM::Role
    Properties:
      Description: Role Bedrock assumes to write model invocation logs.
      AssumeRolePolicyDocument:
        Version: "2012-10-17"
        Statement:
          - Effect: Allow
            Principal:
              Service: bedrock.amazonaws.com
            Action: sts:AssumeRole
            Condition:
              StringEquals:
                aws:SourceAccount: !Ref AWS::AccountId
              ArnLike:
                aws:SourceArn: !Sub "arn:${AWS::Partition}:bedrock:${AWS::Region}:${AWS::AccountId}:*"
      Policies:
        - PolicyName: write-invocation-logs
          PolicyDocument:
            Version: "2012-10-17"
            Statement:
              # Built from its parts rather than from the log group's Arn
              # attribute. That attribute ends in ":*", so appending
              # ":log-stream:..." to it yields an ARN that matches no stream,
              # and PutModelInvocationLoggingConfiguration rejects the role.
              # The form below is the one the Bedrock user guide specifies.
              - Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - logs:CreateLogStream
                  - logs:PutLogEvents
                Resource: !Sub "arn:${AWS::Partition}:logs:${AWS::Region}:${AWS::AccountId}:log-group:${InvocationLogGroup}:log-stream:aws/bedrock/modelinvocations"
      Tags:
        - Key: WorkshopResource
          Value: graphrag-with-neo4j

  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # The backstop budget.
  #
  # A budget alert is not a stop. It sends mail. Cost data refreshes on the order
  # of every eight to twelve hours, so this control will not fire during a
  # four-hour class and is not meant to. It is the line that catches what the
  # breaker missed, read the morning after.
  #
  # Notifications go to email only, never to the breaker topic. Wiring stale cost
  # data to an automatic deactivation would let yesterday's spend switch off
  # today's class.
  #
  # The filter names two Cost Explorer service values and covers the whole
  # account, so unrelated work under either value counts toward it. Read the
  # account's month-to-date spend under those two values before class and treat
  # the class allowance as an increment on that baseline.
  # -------------------------------------------------------------------------

  BackstopBudget:
    Type: AWS::Budgets::Budget
    Properties:
      Budget:
        BudgetName: !Sub "${AWS::StackName}-bedrock-backstop"
        BudgetType: COST
        TimeUnit: MONTHLY
        BudgetLimit:
          Amount: !Ref MonthlyBudgetUsd
          Unit: USD
        CostFilters:
          Service: !Ref BudgetServiceFilters
      NotificationsWithSubscribers:
        - Notification:
            NotificationType: ACTUAL
            ComparisonOperator: GREATER_THAN
            ThresholdType: PERCENTAGE
            Threshold: 50
          Subscribers:
            - SubscriptionType: EMAIL
              Address: !Ref AlertEmail
        - Notification:
            NotificationType: ACTUAL
            ComparisonOperator: GREATER_THAN
            ThresholdType: PERCENTAGE
            Threshold: 80
          Subscribers:
            - SubscriptionType: EMAIL
              Address: !Ref AlertEmail
        - Notification:
            NotificationType: ACTUAL
            ComparisonOperator: GREATER_THAN
            ThresholdType: PERCENTAGE
            Threshold: 100
          Subscribers:
            - SubscriptionType: EMAIL
              Address: !Ref AlertEmail
        - Notification:
            NotificationType: FORECASTED
            ComparisonOperator: GREATER_THAN
            ThresholdType: PERCENTAGE
            Threshold: 100
          Subscribers:
            - SubscriptionType: EMAIL
              Address: !Ref AlertEmail

Outputs:

  BreakerTopicArn:
    Description: Alarm action target.
    Value: !Ref BreakerTopic

  BreakerFunctionName:
    Description: Lambda that deactivates the credential.
    Value: !Ref BreakerFunction

  BurstAlarmName:
    Description: One-minute breaker alarm.
    Value: !Ref BurstSpendAlarm

  SustainedAlarmName:
    Description: Slow-burn breaker alarm.
    Value: !Ref SustainedSpendAlarm

  WorkshopTotalAlarmName:
    Description: Rolling four-hour total-spend breaker alarm.
    Value: !Ref WorkshopTotalSpendAlarm

  BreakerFailureAlarmName:
    Description: >-
      Fires when the breaker Lambda itself errors. Mails the operator and takes
      no other action.
    Value: !Ref BreakerFailureAlarm

  InvocationLogGroupName:
    Description: Log group that will hold prompts and completions.
    Value: !Ref InvocationLogGroup

  InvocationLogRoleArn:
    Description: >-
      Role ARN that admin.py passes to
      bedrock put-model-invocation-logging-configuration.
    Value: !GetAtt InvocationLogRole.Arn

  DashboardUrl:
    Description: The class-day view.
    Value: !Sub "https://${AWS::Region}.console.aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/home?region=${AWS::Region}#dashboards/dashboard/${AWS::StackName}"
